-- The safety-and-populations swarm (2026-08-25). Owner: "lets research
-- every gap or caution you've found... Send a swarm to collect."
--
-- Sixteen agents. Four chased PUBLISHED authorities on the open web
-- (NSCA Long-Term Athletic Development, the ACSM pre-participation
-- screening algorithm, return-to-sport consensus statements, and
-- disordered-eating / low-energy-availability screening); twelve read
-- 80 title-routed transcripts against five new briefs.
--
-- Five new practitioner areas -- clinical, youth, masters, female,
-- detraining -- plus more rows in the guideline area, which stays
-- separate so Coach can weight position stands above video content and
-- cite them by name.
--
-- Two results worth recording next to the data:
--
--   * The FEMALE wave returned ZERO strong-confidence findings. Its
--     brief warned that cycle-based programming is commercially popular
--     and scientifically contested and told analysts to downgrade
--     aggressively; the confidence distribution shows they did. So the
--     generator will not hard-code a lower-body bias or cycle-phase
--     periodisation as science. Per the owner: if an athlete WANTS
--     either, we honour it as a stated preference -- the same doctrine
--     splitPreference already follows, where an explicit choice beats
--     the science ladder.
--
--   * The DETRAINING wave was the densest per video of the whole swarm
--     and directly answers a live defect: our trainingAge is stated and
--     never decays. Its most encodable claims -- return duration roughly
--     equals layoff duration, set return loads by RPE 5-6 rather than a
--     percentage of old maxes, undershoot rather than overshoot because
--     undershooting still buys the repeated-bout protection -- are the
--     evidence behind the generator change shipping alongside this.

